E0009 — deleted spelling

This spelling was deleted: a borrow is written with the sigil of the call site.

A borrow is spelled `x : &T` (read-only) or `x : &mut T` (exclusive) in every slot that holds one: a parameter, a receiver (`self : &Self`), a closure parameter, an `Fn(...)` slot, a local borrow (`y := &place`, `y := &mut place`), a capture list (`{ &y, z : &mut p }`) and the borrowed loop (`for(&mut xs, x => ...)`). The mode words `imm(x)`, `mut(x)` and the older `inout(x)` were deleted (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md decision 42), as was `own(x)`, now `sink(x)`. `yo fix <path> --migrate borrow-spelling` rewrites the borrow words in a whole tree, and `yo fix <path> --migrate modes` rewrites `own`.

Example — this fails:
  { String } :: import("std/string");
  len_of :: (fn(imm(s) : String) -> usize)(s.len());
  export(len_of);
  
Example — write this instead:
  { String } :: import("std/string");
  len_of :: (fn(s : &String) -> usize)(s.len());
  export(len_of);
  
  `imm(s) : String` is the deleted mode-word spelling of the read-only borrow `s : &String`.
Run 'yo explain --list' for all codes.
